      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Which statement is equivalent to $(H∧¬P)∨(K∧¬P)?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we can factor out the conjunction with $¬P,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n(H∧¬P)∨(K∧¬P)≡(H∨K)∧¬P\n$$\n\nThen, we can write\n\n$$\n(H∨K)∧¬P≡¬P∧(H∨K).\n$$",
