      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "Which statement is equivalent to $(A∨B)∧(A∨C)?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we can factor out the disjunction with $A,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n(A∨B)∧(A∨C)≡A∨(B∧C)\n$$\n\nThen, we can write\n\n$$\nA∨(B∧C)≡(B∧C)∨A.\n$$",
