      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "Which statement is equivalent to $(¬P∨R)∧(¬P∨Q)?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we can factor out the disjunction with $¬P,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n(¬P∨R)∧(¬P∨Q)≡¬P∨(R∧Q)\n$$\n\nThen, we can write\n\n$$\n¬P∨(R∧Q)≡(R∧Q)∨¬P.\n$$",
